THIS IS AN EXPERIMENTAL SOURCE-AVAILABLE LICENSE DRAFT. IT IS NOT AN OSI-APPROVED OPEN SOURCE LICENSE. IT HAS NOT YET COMPLETED THE ECL PRE-1.0 QUALIFIED LEGAL-REVIEW GATE AND SHOULD NOT BE RELIED UPON FOR HIGH-CONSEQUENCE DEPLOYMENTS WITHOUT QUALIFIED LEGAL ADVICE.

1. PURPOSE

The Exergic Commons License ("ECL") grants broad permission to exercise copyright and other software rights controlled by a Licensor while withholding that permission where the exercise of those rights materially enables specified forms of coercive capture, systemic domination, deceptive manipulation, repressive surveillance, unlawful political repression, or comparable reductions of meaningful human agency.

The ethical principles motivating this License are described in `spec/PRINCIPLES.md`. Those principles aid interpretation but do not independently create restrictions beyond the operative terms of this License, the exact Restricted Parties Schedule incorporated by the applicable ECL Bundle, and applicable law.

This License is intended to operate through rights that a Licensor actually owns or is authorized to license. It does not create a copyright prohibition over an act merely by calling that act a Prohibited Use.

2. DEFINITIONS

"Software" means the source code, object code, documentation, and other copyrightable material to which a copyright holder or other authorized rightsholder has applied this License.

"Licensor" means a copyright holder or other person or entity authorized to grant one or more Licensed Rights in the Software. Each Licensor acts only with respect to rights that Licensor owns or is authorized to license.

"You" means the individual or legal entity exercising Licensed Rights under this License.

"Licensed Rights" means only those copyright, software-exploitation, and equivalent rights in the Software that a particular Licensor owns or is authorized to license and for which applicable law requires that Licensor's permission. Depending on the applicable law and facts, Licensed Rights may include reproduction; translation, adaptation, arrangement, modification, or creation of derivative works; distribution; and loading, displaying, running, transmission, or storage to the extent those acts require an authorization controlled by the Licensor. Licensed Rights do not include patent or trademark rights and do not include an act to the extent applicable law permits that act without the Licensor's authorization notwithstanding this License.

"Control" means the direct or indirect power to direct the management or policies of an entity, whether through ownership of voting interests, contract, appointment rights, or comparable means.

"Restricted Party", with respect to a particular Licensor's grant or a particular exercise of Licensed Rights, means a person, legal entity, governmental body, agency, military body, or other organization expressly designated in the exact Restricted Parties Schedule contained in the exact ECL Bundle governing that Licensor's grant for the relevant material and Software release. Restricted Party status is grant- and Bundle-relative: designation in one Licensor's Bundle does not by itself designate the same person or entity under another Licensor's grant or Bundle.

"Covered Associate" means, solely in relation to a particular use or project and the exact ECL Bundle governing the Licensed Rights at issue, a person or entity that You know or reasonably should know is materially acting for, under the direction or Control of, on behalf of, or for the material benefit of a Restricted Party under that same Bundle. Covered Associate includes a contractor, consultant, controlled affiliate, material project collaborator, intermediary, or service provider when the relevant activity materially supports such a Restricted Party. Mere historical contact, incidental interaction, ordinary consumer use, or remote social association does not by itself create Covered Associate status.

"Material Participation" means participation that makes a non-trivial contribution to the design, financing, governance, development, training, operation, deployment, commercialization, targeting, decision-making, or material outputs of a project.

"Restricted Project", with respect to a particular Licensor's grant or a particular exercise of Licensed Rights, means a project, program, deployment, contract, research effort, service, product, or coordinated activity that, under the exact ECL Bundle governing those Licensed Rights, either:

(a) is expressly designated as a Restricted Project in the exact Restricted Parties Schedule contained in that Bundle;
(b) has Material Participation by a Restricted Party as resolved under that Bundle;
(c) has Material Participation by a Covered Associate in connection with such a Restricted Party;
(d) is performed at the direction of, on behalf of, or primarily for the material benefit of such a Restricted Party; or
(e) is structured through an intermediary, contractor, consortium, affiliate, or other arrangement with the purpose or substantial effect of avoiding a restriction that governs the same Licensor's grant and Bundle.

A project does not become a Restricted Project solely because an unrelated participant has an incidental or unknown connection to a Restricted Party. Restricted Project status is grant- and Bundle-relative: status under one Bundle does not by itself make the project Restricted under another Licensor's grant or Bundle.

"Restricted Parties Schedule" or "Schedule" means the exact immutable versioned document incorporated by a particular ECL Bundle governing a particular Licensor's grant for particular ECL-covered material and Software release, listing Restricted Parties, Restricted Projects, and any expressly defined class-based designations or exclusions for that Bundle. A Software release may contain material governed by more than one ECL Bundle; each Schedule resolves only for the grant and material governed by its own Bundle. The Schedule must be objectively identifiable by an immutable version, content hash, or exact ECL Bundle manifest. A mutable branch, `latest` page, registry view, or channel pointer is not by itself an incorporated Schedule. A later Schedule never retroactively alters the Licensed Rights or restrictions attached to an earlier grant and Bundle; adopting a different Schedule requires a new exact ECL Bundle for the affected Licensor's new Software release or release of affected material.

"Canonical Empty Schedule" means the immutable Schedule artifact `ECL-RP-EMPTY-1` stored as `schedules/ECL-RP-EMPTY-1.md`, whose SHA-256 is `e12a6ffc03aa0be24a9f61d0d325bc8c06bb9c870416a72fcac0bfd968025aa2`. It intentionally contains no Restricted Parties, Restricted Projects, class-based designations, or exclusions and may be used only by the limited original-Licensor fallback in Section 4.

"ECL Bundle" or "Bundle" means the exact combination of the ECL License version and exact Restricted Parties Schedule governing a particular Licensor's grant in particular ECL-covered material and Software release, identified by an immutable manifest or equivalent release metadata that pins the relevant artifacts and their cryptographic hashes. A combined Software release may therefore contain more than one ECL Bundle, and each Bundle remains associated with the Licensor grant and material it governs. Where the Section 4 original-Licensor fallback applies, the exact fallback Bundle is deterministically the tuple consisting of the objectively identifiable exact ECL License artifact and its SHA-256 plus the Canonical Empty Schedule identifier and SHA-256; an absent original manifest does not make that fallback Bundle mutable or permit substitution of another Schedule.

"Prohibited Use" means a use context described in Section 5 in which particular Licensed Rights may not be exercised under the relevant Licensor's grant and exact ECL Bundle as provided by that Section.

"Independent Remediation Activity" means an activity whose principal and actual purpose is to investigate, document, challenge, audit, review, prosecute, defend against, remedy, disclose, or prevent a Prohibited Use or the conduct forming the basis of a Restricted Party or Restricted Project designation under the exact Bundle relevant to the Licensed Rights at issue, provided that the relevant person or function:

(a) is operationally independent from the persons or functions directing or materially participating in the underlying prohibited conduct;
(b) does not itself materially participate in that conduct except in an investigative, judicial, defence, audit, oversight, disclosure, or remedial capacity;
(c) does not exercise Licensed Rights to continue, conceal, optimize, or materially support the underlying Prohibited Use or Restricted Project; and
(d) limits exercise of Licensed Rights to what is reasonably necessary for the remedial purpose.

3. GRANT OF LICENSED RIGHTS

Subject only to the conditions that this License expressly places on Licensed Rights under the particular Licensor's grant and exact ECL Bundle — including Section 4, Section 5, and the Licensed-Rights restrictions in Section 6 other than the Hosted-Service Covenant — each Licensor grants You a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive license to exercise all Licensed Rights that the particular Licensor owns or is authorized to license in the Software. The Hosted-Service Covenant is not part of this grant qualifier and does not limit, suspend, condition, or terminate Licensed Rights merely by being incorporated in this License.

Accordingly, to the extent a relevant act requires a Licensed Right, this grant permits You to reproduce, load, run, inspect, study, modify, adapt, translate, combine, create derivative works from, distribute, deploy, and provide services using the Software, subject only to conditions that expressly govern those Licensed Rights under that Licensor's grant and exact Bundle and not to the Hosted-Service Covenant as such.

You may exercise Licensed Rights for personal, academic, scientific, educational, governmental, non-profit, or commercial purposes except where that exercise independently violates a condition on those Licensed Rights in Section 5 or the Licensed-Rights restrictions in Section 6 under the exact Bundle governing the affected Licensor's grant, or forms part of a Restricted Project as resolved under that same Bundle in circumstances that involve exercise of those Licensed Rights. Noncompliance with the Hosted-Service Covenant alone does not remove this permission.

Section 4, Section 5, and the Licensed-Rights restrictions in Section 6 other than the Hosted-Service Covenant are conditions on the Licensed Rights granted by this Section only to the extent they govern the particular Licensor's grant, material, and exact ECL Bundle at issue. The Hosted-Service Covenant is not a condition of the copyright or software-right grant and is governed only by the separate contractual basis expressly stated in Section 6. If an activity does not exercise a Licensed Right and does not otherwise require a Licensor's authorization under applicable law, this License does not transform that activity into copyright infringement merely because the activity falls within a factual description used by this License.

This License does not assume that an independent contract has been formed for conduct outside the Licensed Rights. Section 6 describes a separate Hosted-Service Covenant for the narrow service-provider gap identified there, but that covenant exists for a particular Licensor and Bundle only where the operative license text in that exact Bundle actually contains the covenant and applicable law finds an independently sufficient contractual basis for that same Licensor, Bundle, and materially used ECL-covered material, including any required formation, notice, assent, authority, consideration or other legal basis, and enforceability. Contract formation or assent associated only with another Licensor or another Bundle does not create this covenant for the affected grant. No contractual obligation or remedy beyond the Licensed Rights arises merely because this License labels conduct restricted.

4. DISTRIBUTION AND BUNDLE-PRESERVATION CONDITIONS

If You distribute ECL-covered material, modified or unmodified, in exercise of Licensed Rights granted by one or more Licensors, the following duties apply separately to each relevant Licensor's grant, the material governed by that grant, and its exact ECL Bundle. For each such grant and material, You must:

(a) preserve copyright, attribution, and license notices applicable to that material and grant;
(b) provide a copy of this License or an unambiguous immutable reference to the exact ECL License version governing that material and grant;
(c) provide the exact Schedule contained in the exact ECL Bundle governing that material and grant in a form that accompanies the distributed copy and allows the recipient to read the operative Restricted Party, Restricted Project, class-designation, and exclusion entries without consulting mutable project state;
(d) preserve and provide immutable Bundle metadata identifying the exact License and exact Schedule governing that material and grant, including their immutable versions or identifiers and cryptographic hashes, so the recipient can verify which artifacts govern that material without consulting a mutable `latest`, branch, registry view, or channel;
(e) identify material modifications made by You to that material; and
(f) not represent the Software as OSI-approved open source unless a future version has separately received such approval.

A Bundle manifest, hash, repository-relative path, or other identifier may verify the Schedule supplied under paragraph (c), but does not by itself substitute for providing the operative Schedule. A distributor may instead provide a demonstrably retrievable immutable content-addressed copy only where the reference itself remains sufficient for the recipient to retrieve and read the exact Schedule independently of any mutable branch, channel, registry view, repository-relative path, or later project state.

The Section 4 duties and breaches are several by Licensor grant, material, and exact Bundle. A failure to preserve or provide a Schedule, Bundle, notice, or other required information for one Licensor's grant or material breaches this Section only with respect to the Licensed Rights exercised under that affected Licensor's grant for that affected material and Bundle. Such a failure does not by itself breach, condition, narrow, or terminate another Licensor's otherwise-compliant grant merely because the materials were distributed together.

For an original application of ECL by a Licensor to material over which that Licensor controls the relevant Licensed Rights, the fallback in this paragraph applies only if the exact ECL License artifact or version governing that Licensor's grant is objectively identifiable but that Licensor's own initial release materials fail to identify an exact incorporated Schedule objectively. In that case, the Canonical Empty Schedule is deemed incorporated for **that Licensor's grant in that material and that release only**. The exact fallback Bundle is the deterministic pair of (i) that exact ECL License artifact/version and its SHA-256 and (ii) `ECL-RP-EMPTY-1` with SHA-256 `e12a6ffc03aa0be24a9f61d0d325bc8c06bb9c870416a72fcac0bfd968025aa2`. Those two component identities are sufficient equivalent immutable release metadata for the fallback Bundle even if the original publisher omitted a Bundle manifest. If the exact ECL License artifact/version itself cannot be established, this fallback does not manufacture an exact Bundle or permit a party to substitute a later, mutable, or guessed License or Schedule. This limited fallback does not remove the independent Section 5 conditions governing that Licensor's grant.

The empty-Schedule fallback cannot erase, replace, weaken, or re-resolve an exact upstream Bundle already governing ECL-covered material received from another Licensor. A downstream distributor or modifier must preserve each applicable upstream Schedule and Bundle under paragraphs (c) and (d). Failure to preserve a particular upstream Schedule or Bundle is a breach only as to the upstream grant and material governed by that omitted or corrupted Bundle; it does not make that Schedule empty, does not substitute a later or mutable Schedule, does not expand any downstream recipient's rights in the upstream material, and does not create a breach of another Licensor's otherwise-compliant grant.

You may license Your own original additions under additional terms, provided those terms do not purport to remove or weaken restrictions that continue to apply to ECL-covered material or grant rights in another Licensor's material that You do not possess.

Each downstream recipient who receives ECL-covered material may independently exercise Licensed Rights granted directly by each relevant Licensor under the exact ECL Bundle governing that Licensor's grant for the recipient's copy or release, provided the recipient independently complies with the conditions that Bundle expressly places on those Licensed Rights. The Hosted-Service Covenant, even where separately enforceable as a contract, is not part of that proviso, and covenant-only noncompliance does not limit, suspend, condition, terminate, forfeit, or otherwise narrow the recipient's direct Licensed-Rights grant. A downstream distributor's omission or corruption of required Schedule or Bundle information does not grant the recipient broader rights than the relevant upstream Licensor granted.

5. PROHIBITED USE CONTEXTS — CONDITIONS ON LICENSED RIGHTS

As a condition of each particular Licensor's grant in the exact ECL Bundle governing the Licensed Rights at issue, You may not knowingly exercise any such Licensed Right in or to the Software where that exercise materially enables or supports any of the following. References in this Section to using, deploying, training, integrating, hosting, or otherwise employing the Software describe the factual context of the conditioned exercise of Licensed Rights; they do not assert a freestanding copyright right over conduct that applicable law does not reserve to a Licensor.

5.1 Repressive surveillance.
Systematic surveillance, tracking, identification, or profiling of persons or populations for the purpose of political repression, persecution, unlawful intimidation, arbitrary detention, or suppression of lawful dissent.

5.2 Coercive targeting.
Selection, prioritization, scoring, targeting, or operational support intended to facilitate unlawful violence, torture, enforced disappearance, collective punishment, or intentional attacks against civilians or other persons protected by applicable international law.

5.3 Systematic discriminatory domination.
Automated or data-driven systems whose primary purpose is to impose unlawful discrimination or systematically deny fundamental rights on the basis of protected personal characteristics.

5.4 Deceptive population manipulation.
Large-scale systems primarily designed to deliberately deceive a population about material facts in order to remove meaningful political, civic, or personal agency, excluding ordinary persuasion, advertising, satire, fiction, or clearly disclosed simulation.

5.5 Irreversible coercive capture.
Systems primarily designed to create or maintain coercive technological dependence, informational control, or decision-making asymmetry where affected persons or communities are intentionally denied a meaningful ability to understand, contest, exit, or seek an alternative, and where that denial materially restricts fundamental rights or civic autonomy.

5.6 Systematic coercive domination and unlawful political repression.
Systems, deployments, operational processes, or material Software-enabled capabilities whose primary purpose, or whose known and reasonably foreseeable material function in the relevant deployment, is to enable or maintain systematic persecution, unlawful political repression, torture or comparably severe cruel, inhuman, or degrading treatment, enforced disappearance, arbitrary detention, collective punishment, forced labour, forced displacement or expulsion without meaningful individualized protection, severe discriminatory domination, or a comparable coercive denial of fundamental rights or of the practical ability to dissent, contest, or exit.

Ordinary lawful criminal justice, immigration administration, military service, employment, public-health action, emergency response, content moderation, public administration, or other compulsory activity is not prohibited merely because it is coercive, restrictive, controversial, or governmental. Capital punishment, detention, deportation, conscription, protest regulation, and similar exercises of State power are not standalone ECL categories; the relevant Software-enabled context must independently satisfy the elements of this or another subsection.

5.7 Circumvention.
Exercise of Licensed Rights granted by a particular Licensor under a particular exact ECL Bundle through an arrangement whose principal purpose is to enable conduct that another provision of this License or the Schedule in that same Bundle expressly prohibits with respect to those same Licensed Rights, that same Licensor's grant, and that same Bundle. A prohibition that exists only under another Licensor's grant or Bundle does not by itself satisfy this subsection for the affected grant.

A context is not prohibited merely because it is controversial, politically disputed, military-adjacent, commercial, governmental, security-related, or capable of dual use. The relevant exercise of Licensed Rights must satisfy the substantive criteria above under the affected Licensor's grant and exact Bundle or fall within a Restricted Project as resolved under that same Bundle.

6. RESTRICTED PARTIES, PROJECTS, AND SERVICE PROVISION

For every Licensed-Rights condition in this Section, Restricted Party, Covered Associate, and Restricted Project status must be resolved against the exact ECL Bundle governing the particular Licensor's grant and Licensed Rights at issue. A designation or status under another Licensor's Bundle does not by itself withhold, condition, narrow, or terminate this Licensor's grant.

No Licensed Rights are granted by a particular Licensor under a particular exact ECL Bundle to a Restricted Party as determined under that same Bundle, except to the limited extent expressly permitted by the Independent Remediation Activity provision below. This withholding applies only to rights that Licensor is legally entitled to withhold under that grant and Bundle and does not purport to negate statutory rights, exhausted rights, or other permissions that applicable law makes available independently of this License. A Restricted Party designation in another Bundle does not by itself withhold this grant.

You may not knowingly exercise Licensed Rights granted by a particular Licensor under an exact ECL Bundle as part of a Restricted Project determined under that same Bundle.

You may not knowingly exercise any Licensed Right granted by a particular Licensor under an exact ECL Bundle to reproduce, adapt, modify, configure where configuration constitutes adaptation, distribute, install, deploy where deployment requires reproduction, update, scale where scaling requires reproduction, transmit where transmission implicates a Licensed Right, or otherwise provision or maintain the Software for the purpose of providing a Restricted Party or Restricted Project as determined under that same Bundle with the Software, a derivative work, hosted functionality, integration, model, dataset transformation, technical service, or other material Software-enabled capability where You know or reasonably should know that the exercise of that Licensed Right materially enables or supports that Restricted Party or Restricted Project.

For avoidance of doubt, where You operate the Software to provide remote or hosted functionality, this Section first conditions the provider's **actual exercise of Licensed Rights** under each affected Licensor's grant and exact Bundle in establishing, provisioning, modifying, updating, scaling, or maintaining the service. A remote user who merely receives functionality or output and does not itself exercise a Licensed Right is not deemed a copyright licensee solely because it used the remote service.

A provider may have lawfully established a long-lived or multi-tenant deployment before it knows that a later customer is a Restricted Party or that a later use is part of a Restricted Project under a relevant exact Bundle. If, after that knowledge arises, continued service from the already established deployment can occur without any further exercise of a Licensed Right, this License does **not** deem the later service request itself an exercise of copyright or another Licensed Right merely to manufacture an infringement theory.

To address that service-provider gap without inventing a copyright-exclusive right, the following **Hosted-Service Covenant** is Bundle-specific. It applies with respect to a particular Licensor's grant, exact ECL Bundle, and ECL-covered material only if (i) the operative ECL License text contained in that exact Bundle actually includes this Hosted-Service Covenant and (ii) applicable law recognizes an independently enforceable contract or other independently sufficient contractual basis incorporating that covenant with respect to that same Licensor, Bundle, and material. Formation, notice, assent, authority, consideration, acceptance of ECL-granted rights, or any other contractual basis associated only with Licensor A or Bundle A does not establish the covenant for Licensor B or Bundle B. An older or different Bundle whose operative License text does not contain this covenant has no Hosted-Service Covenant merely because its material is used in a combined hosted deployment.

Where those Bundle-specific requirements are satisfied, You covenant that after You know or reasonably should know that a customer, beneficiary, project, or materially supported activity is a Restricted Party or Restricted Project under that same Bundle, You will not knowingly continue to provide that party or project with material Software-enabled hosted functionality or capability materially enabled by ECL-covered material governed by that Bundle, except to the extent permitted as an Independent Remediation Activity. A designation under one Bundle may support only the independently formed contractual covenant obligation associated with that same Bundle and material; it does not create a covenant for, or alter Licensed Rights under, another Licensor's grant or Bundle.

The Hosted-Service Covenant is deliberately contractual and is not a condition on Licensed Rights granted by Section 3. Its breach does not by itself constitute copyright infringement or terminate a copyright or other Licensed Right grant where the complained-of conduct does not independently breach a Licensed-Rights condition. Contractual obligations and remedies exist only to the extent the relevant jurisdiction recognizes the required Bundle-specific formation, assent, authority, consideration or other legal basis, enforceability, and remedy. Any remedy for a covenant-only breach must operate without limiting, suspending, conditioning, rescinding, terminating, forfeiting, or otherwise altering the existence, scope, continuity, or exercise of Licensed Rights granted by this License; ECL does not incorporate or authorize such a grant-affecting remedy merely because a contract incorporates this covenant. If no independently sufficient contract or contractual basis exists for the particular Licensor and Bundle whose covenant is asserted, the covenant does not apply to that Bundle; ECL reaches the provider under that grant only when and to the extent the provider actually exercises a Licensed Right or another authorization controlled by that Licensor.

A person who is a Covered Associate only because of a professional or project-specific relationship under a particular Bundle is not permanently restricted from unrelated personal or professional activity after that relationship ceases, unless that person is separately designated as a Restricted Party in the exact Bundle relevant to the Licensed Rights at issue.

Notwithstanding the preceding restrictions, a person or function otherwise within the scope of a Restricted Party under the relevant exact Bundle may exercise Licensed Rights under that same Licensor's grant and Bundle solely to conduct an Independent Remediation Activity. This exception may apply, where its definition is actually satisfied, to an independent court or tribunal, ombuds or National Preventive Mechanism function, inspector, auditor, prosecutor investigating official abuse, independent legal defence function, public-interest accountability body, or comparable remedial function.

A person relying on this exception must have reasonably documented grounds for concluding that the Independent Remediation Activity definition is satisfied. The exception does not authorize ordinary operational, intelligence, military, policing, detention, immigration, procurement, surveillance, targeting, administrative, or commercial activity merely because it is described as compliance, oversight, safety, accountability, or remediation.

7. KNOWLEDGE STANDARD

Except for a person or entity expressly designated as a Restricted Party, or a project expressly designated as a Restricted Project, under the exact Bundle governing the affected Licensor's grant, restrictions based on association, participation, benefit, or project status apply where You actually know, or where a reasonable person in Your position would have substantial grounds to know, the facts creating the restriction under that Bundle.

You are not required to conduct unlimited investigations into remote ownership chains, unknown collaborators, passive investors, or undisclosed relationships. Deliberate avoidance of readily available facts does not defeat this Section.

8. GOVERNANCE AND DESIGNATIONS

The repository maintaining ECL should publish a governance procedure describing how Restricted Parties and Restricted Projects are proposed, evaluated, challenged, reviewed, added, narrowed, or removed.

A Schedule designation should be based on documented evidence and a reasoned conclusion that the designated party or project materially and systematically participates in, directs, enables, or derives substantial benefit from conduct substantially matching one or more Section 5 criteria, or deliberately circumvents an ECL restriction. Mere political disagreement, nationality, ethnicity, religion, ideology, military status, commercial size, or remote association is insufficient.

A designation should identify the narrowest reasonably knowable actor, project, apparatus, or determinable class supported by the evidence and should state material exclusions or remedial functions where necessary to avoid overbreadth.

For license-compliance purposes, however, an express designation or exclusion in the exact Schedule contained in the exact ECL Bundle governing the particular Licensor's grant controls only for that grant and Bundle. A licensee is not required to independently re-litigate the evidentiary basis for every Schedule entry in order to determine whether the entry applies, but an entry in one Bundle does not become operative for another Licensor's grant merely because the covered materials appear in the same Software release.

The governance procedure and supporting evidence do not themselves modify the operative license attached to a Licensor's grant or Software release. A designation becomes binding for a particular Licensor's grant only through the exact Schedule contained in the exact ECL Bundle governing that grant and material.

9. NON-RETROACTIVITY AND IMMUTABLE RELEASE STATE

Once a Licensor releases particular ECL-covered material under a specific ECL Bundle, later amendments to ECL, the Schedule, governance records, evidence, registry views, channels, or classifications do not retroactively alter the Licensed Rights or restrictions attached to that Licensor's grant and released Bundle.

A new Software release or release of affected material may adopt a later ECL License version or Schedule for a particular Licensor's grant by creating or resolving a new exact Bundle for that grant and material.

A combined Software release may contain multiple immutable ECL Bundles. Moving a mutable channel such as `stable`, `stable-1`, `candidate`, or `draft`, or changing another Licensor's Bundle, does not change the Bundle already attached to an earlier grant or released material.

10. TERMINATION, AUTHORITY, AND REINSTATEMENT

Rights granted by a particular Licensor under this License terminate only with respect to the Licensed Rights that particular Licensor granted, only for a breach that independently violates a condition governing those same Licensed Rights under that Licensor's identified grant, Software release, and exact ECL Bundle, and only as provided by this Section. Notice may be given by that Licensor or by a person or entity the Licensor has authorized to administer or enforce the relevant grant. One Licensor does not, merely by being a Licensor, have authority to terminate rights granted by another Licensor. A breach involving only Licensed Rights granted by another Licensor, another Software release, or another Bundle is not a basis to terminate this Licensor's grant unless the same conduct independently breaches a condition governing this Licensor's own identified grant and Bundle.

A notice intended to trigger termination under this Section must identify with reasonable specificity: (a) the affected Licensor or Licensors whose grant is asserted to be terminable; (b) the ECL-covered material, contribution, or other objectively identifiable portion of Software to which that grant relates; (c) the affected Software release and exact ECL Bundle, including the two component hashes where the Canonical Empty Schedule fallback defines that Bundle; (d) the Licensed Rights or grant whose termination is asserted; (e) the material breach, the facts reasonably sufficient to understand it, and how those facts independently violate a condition governing Licensed Rights under each affected Licensor's identified grant, release, and Bundle; (f) the authority of the notifying party to act for each affected Licensor; and (g) any applicable cure deadline. Where a notice concerns more than one Licensor, it must establish the breach-to-grant connection separately for each affected Licensor. If the affected release and exact Bundle cannot be established with reasonable specificity, or if the notice does not establish how the alleged breach attaches to the affected Licensor's identified grant and Bundle, the notice is insufficient to terminate that grant under this Section until those matters are established. Missing, omitted, unavailable, or corrupted release or Bundle metadata does not broaden the scope of termination and does not permit the notifier to substitute a mutable or later Bundle. A notice does not terminate rights beyond the affected grant, material, release, Bundle, and Licensor scope that it objectively identifies.

For a knowing violation of Section 5 or of a Licensed-Rights restriction in Section 6 other than the Hosted-Service Covenant, the affected Licensor's identified grant terminates with respect to the identified affected Software only if the violation independently breaches a condition governing Licensed Rights granted by that affected Licensor under that identified grant, Software release, and exact ECL Bundle, and You fail to cease and cure the violation within thirty (30) days after receiving a notice satisfying the preceding paragraph. For deliberate circumvention under Section 5.7, termination of the identified affected grant may take effect upon such notice without a cure period only where the circumvention independently breaches a condition governing that same affected Licensor's identified grant and Bundle.

For any other material breach of a condition on Licensed Rights, the affected Licensor's identified grant terminates only if that condition governs Licensed Rights under that affected Licensor's identified grant, Software release, and exact ECL Bundle, and You fail to cure the breach within thirty (30) days after receiving a notice satisfying the notice requirements above.

Termination is limited to rights actually granted by the affected Licensor, under the identified grant and exact Bundle, and objectively identified by the terminating notice. It does not itself transfer, extinguish, or terminate rights owned or independently granted by another rightsholder, another Bundle, another Software release, or material outside the identified affected grant. Conduct that breaches another Licensor's condition but does not independently breach a condition governing the affected Licensor's identified grant cannot be used as a cross-grant termination trigger.

A downstream recipient who obtained an ECL-covered copy before Your termination and who holds an independent direct grant from the relevant Licensor remains governed by that recipient's own compliance with conditions on Licensed Rights under that Licensor's exact Bundle and is not automatically terminated solely because Your grant terminated or because that recipient breaches only the Hosted-Service Covenant.

After termination, rights from the affected Licensor are reinstated only if that Licensor or an authorized enforcement agent expressly reinstates them, unless applicable law requires a different result. A reinstatement may be unconditional or subject to lawful written conditions. Cure before the applicable termination deadline prevents termination under the relevant notice.

A breach of the Hosted-Service Covenant described in Section 6 does not limit, suspend, condition, rescind, terminate, forfeit, or otherwise alter any copyright, software-right, or other Licensed Right grant under this License, whether directly under this License or indirectly through a contractual remedy. Its consequences are limited to remedies available, if any, under the independently enforceable Bundle-specific contract or contractual basis that validly incorporates that covenant and that operate without altering the existence, scope, continuity, or exercise of Licensed Rights. Rescission, suspension, termination, forfeiture, or any other grant-affecting remedy is not a remedy supplied or incorporated by the Hosted-Service Covenant for covenant-only breach. A separately negotiated agreement may contain independent terms to the extent enforceable under applicable law, but no such grant-affecting term arises merely from incorporating ECL or the Hosted-Service Covenant and no such separate term constitutes termination under this Section. If the same conduct independently breaches a condition on Licensed Rights, termination may occur only on the basis of that separate Licensed-Rights breach, only with respect to the Licensor grant and Bundle whose condition that conduct independently breached, and only under the notice, scope, and cure rules of this Section.

11. STATUTORY RIGHTS, EXCEPTIONS, EXHAUSTION, AND MANDATORY LAW

Nothing in this License restricts an act to the extent applicable law permits that act without authorization from the relevant Licensor notwithstanding the terms of this License, or makes the relevant statutory right, exception, limitation, or privilege non-waivable.

An act performed solely under such an independent statutory permission is not an exercise of Licensed Rights granted by this License merely because the Software is involved.

Nothing in this License is intended to recreate a copyright distribution right that applicable law has exhausted with respect to a particular copy. Exhaustion of a distribution right does not by itself grant permission to reproduce, adapt, modify, or otherwise exercise a distinct Licensed Right that remains controlled by a Licensor.

Nothing in this Section determines whether a waivable statutory default may be altered by a separately valid contract. ECL does not rely on an assumed contract outside the Licensed Rights except for the Hosted-Service Covenant described in Section 6, and that covenant applies for a particular Licensor and exact Bundle only where the operative License text in that Bundle contains the covenant and an independently enforceable Bundle-specific contract or other independently sufficient contractual basis incorporating it is formed under applicable law.

